// Formatter config. oxfmt replaced Prettier; these are the four settings the
// repository formatted under before the move, carried over unchanged, so the
// switch changed layout only where the two tools genuinely disagree.
// See docs/spikes/oxfmt-trial.md for the measurements that led here.
//
// Named `.oxfmtrc.json` rather than `oxfmt.config.mjs` deliberately. Only the
// `.oxfmtrc.*` names are auto-discovered, so a bare `oxfmt` run — by a human, an editor
// extension, or an agent — picks these settings up. A config reachable only via `-c`
// would let a bare run fall through to oxfmt's own defaults (semicolons, double quotes)
// and rewrite the entire repository.
//
// There is deliberately no `ignorePatterns` block, even though `--migrate` emits one:
// oxfmt reads `.prettierignore` and `.gitignore` natively. Duplicating the list would
// give the byte-exact exclusions a second copy to drift out of sync with — the vendored
// upstream schemas, the hook payload snapshots, and the generated headless contract are
// all drift-checked against their exact bytes, so a stale second ignore list is the one
// failure mode that matters here. Verified equivalent: the same file set is scanned
// with and without the duplicated block.
{
  // Carried over verbatim from the former prettier.config.mjs.
  "semi": false,
  "singleQuote": true,
  "printWidth": 100,
  "trailingComma": "all",

  // Not a formatting setting, and it defaults to ON. Left off deliberately: enabled,
  // oxfmt re-sorts the keys of every package.json it finds — the root manifest,
  // packages/extract-zip, and benchmarks/steer/fixtures/injection-project, whose bytes
  // are part of the steer-eval corpus rather than project source. Turning it on is a
  // separate decision from which formatter runs.
  "sortPackageJson": false
}
